From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Turn the hang watcher off by default on Windows

Default EnableHangWatcher to disabled on Windows: no HangWatcher thread
in each process. Social Club replaces the browser's --disable-features for its children,
so a switch cannot do this; a compiled default it never names can.
(PLA-384).
Apply after the pinned CEF stock patches.

Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-17-cef-trim.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 base/threading/hang_watcher.cc |    5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/base/threading/hang_watcher.cc b/base/threading/hang_watcher.cc
index 348b2134ed..232b3e436a 100644
--- a/base/threading/hang_watcher.cc
+++ b/base/threading/hang_watcher.cc
@@ -239,9 +239,10 @@ bool ThreadTypeLoggingLevelGreaterOrEqual(HangWatcher::ThreadType thread_type,
 // Enables the HangWatcher. When disabled, the HangWatcher thread should not be
 // started. Enabled by default only on platforms where the generated data is
 // used, to avoid unnecessary overhead.
+// Off on Windows: an embedder that must fit several processes in a small
+// address space runs no watcher thread in each.
 BASE_FEATURE(kEnableHangWatcher,
-#if BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN) || BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC) || BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS) || \
-    BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX)
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC) || BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS) || BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX)
              FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT
 #else
              FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT
